{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/633136-the-king-has-left-the-building-101-famous-changeling-plothooks","id":633136,"title":"The King Has Left The Building (101 Famous Changeling Plothooks)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-19T23:00:03-07:00","id":633136,"title":"The King Has Left The Building (101 Famous Changeling Plothooks)","content":"So I was reading through one of my favourite books to get modern adventure seeds from, which is entitled The Little Book of Conspiracies. This time, I was drawn to one of the most enduring conspiracies of our time: the belief that Elvis faked his death, and that the body within his open casket was a wax dummy. With that came a few ideas for Changeling stories you could tell. <br /> <br /> 1) Elvis never died. The True Fae are masters at creating duplicates of the living, so some have learned how to duplicate a corpse as well. Mr Presley is still trapped in Arcadia, serving in the role of both the King and the Bard, but it's anyone's guess who's court he is in. <br /> <br /> 2) The body in the casket was actually Elvis' Fetch, held together a little longer by a Contract with Death itself. The catch? The fetch wasn't murdered by the real Elvis, who now hops from Freehold to Freehold, trying to piece together why someone wants him or his fetch murdered.<br /> <br /> 3) The body in the casket was the real, living Elvis, who became a changeling of wax glory and finally managed to use a combination of Wyrd magic and plain old stagecraft to get the peace of a faked death. What he wanted peace from though was not fame, but something darker entirely...<br /> <br /> Please feel free to add other plot hooks involving famous Changelings as you see fit!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T23:41:50-07:00","id":633199,"title":"","content":"Well, if Elvis was captured there is a chance (like 100%) that his mien would look different from his original body. Perhaps he was abducted and became a Fairest. On the other hand it would be tragic for him if he became an Ogre or a Wizened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;A dark shape crawls out from your closet. At first it looks like it has a large zipper for a mouth, however as it gets closer you soon realize that it isn't a zipper at all but rows of sharp yellow teeth!&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7343-werescythe","name":"Werescythe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T11:47:11-07:00","id":633634,"title":"","content":"4) In 71 BC, the Spartacus' army of rebellious slaves was defeated at the Battle of the Siler River. Contrary to modern film portrayals, Spartacus was presumed at the time to have been killed in the fighting, but his body was never found. In reality, the Sparticus who was slain that day was a fetch, and his body disintegrated into a pile of sand and tarnished bronze before a tally of the dead could be made. The real Spartacus had been carried away to Arcadia some time before, to serve as the general of a fey army. Considering his history of rebellion, it seems unlikely that his keeper could hold him forever, but in any case there's surely no way he could still be around more than two thousand years later. Surely.<br /> <br /> 5) The Roanoke Colony, in modern North Carolina, was the subject of one of history's most famous disappearances. In 1587, around 115 colonists arrived on Roanoke island, at the site of a previous failed colony. Discovering that a garrison left behind by a previous expedition had apparently been wiped out, and experiencing almost immediate conflicts with some of the local native Americans, the colonists persuaded the governor to return to England and request aid. A war with Spain delayed the arrival of relief until 1590, when the colony was found abandoned. Remarkably, there were no signs of fighting, and the houses and fortifications appeared to have have been deliberately dismantled, suggesting that the colonists weren't forced to leave in a hurry. The most tantalizing clue regarding the fate of the colonists was the word &quot;CROATOAN,&quot; found carved in a tree at the colony site.<br /> <br /> Many modern experts believe that the colonists, facing starvation and hostility from one group of natives, had abandoned their homes and joined with the Croatan people, who lived on another nearby island. Persistent rumors among American Changelings tell a different story, however, of an isolated community abducted <i>en masse</i> by the True Fae, many of whom may still be held in the timeless depths of some Arcadian realm.<br /> <br /> 6) Henry Every, known to his crew as Long Ben, was perhaps the most notorious pirate of the 17th century. A former sailor of the English navy, he operated for a time as an unlicensed slave trader in the Atlantic, and then as a crewman in a merchant convoy, before seizing control in a mutiny and turning to piracy. In 1695, he seized a Mughal fleet en route to Surat, capturing a fantastic treasure in gold, silver, and jewels in what would become known as piracy's greatest exploit. Every's attack threatened to turn the Mughals firmly against the English East India Company, and as an act of contrition the English launched a global manhunt for the pirates responsible. Every and his crew retired for a time to the Bahamas before being forced to flee, and were discovered trying to unload their treasure at a port in Ireland. After once more fleeing to the sea, Every was never seen again, despite more than a decade of searching.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately for the changelings of the world, the career of the infamous Pirate King didn't end with his disappearance. Not long afterward, rumors began to spread among the Lost of a singularly ruthless and cunning privateer raiding seaside Freeholds around the world and dragging their inhabitants back to Arcadia in the hold of his terrible hedgespun ship. Even three hundred years later, Long Ben remains a bogeyman among changelings in many parts of the globe, with stories claiming that he's still on the hunt, having long since transformed into something altogether inhuman, a living nightmare from a bygone age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 08-20-2015, 06:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T21:38:09-07:00","id":635434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werescythe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/633136-the-king-has-left-the-building-101-famous-changeling-plothooks?p=633199#post633199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, if Elvis was captured there is a chance (like 100%) that his mien would look different from his original body. Perhaps he was abducted and became a Fairest. On the other hand it would be tragic for him if he became an Ogre or a Wizened.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely, but that all depends on what the plot is that the Storyteller wants to create is. It could range from minimal, to tragic, to horrific.<br /> <br /> 7) Most Changelings experience Durance that last for years, often returning decades after they were originally taken by The Others. The shortest that anyone can think of though is a mere 10 days. In December of 1926, Agatha Christie disappear for ten days, apparently suffered amnesia, then resurfaced using the name of her husbands lover. It is whispered in Freeholds around the world that she had been taken by any extremely brash Fae, then for some reason escaped immediately. There are rumours even that from her point of veiw, she was gone not even an hour! Either way, no Fetch appeared, and she was in Arcadia for such a short time that her Mein is almost identical to her human appearance. Everyone has to ask though, which Fae could have been so bold too abduct someone so well known... And why did they let her go so easily?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0